Feature: Outcome-Label Sidecar
  As a dataset-harvest consumer (QAV/coach harvest transforms, the WS4-S7 Chronicler)
  I want disposition verdicts recorded as structured label records adjacent to the evidence they judge, at judgment time
  So that harvests join outcome labels by file read instead of retro archaeology

  Background:
    Given a completed autobuild run has produced evidence artifacts for a task
    And the task's evidence directory is present on this node

  # ── GROUP A: Key Examples ──

  # Why: Core path — the "labels for free" moment: a review disposition immediately produces a label record
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] Disposition commands write labels automatically; a manual CLI covers operator_caught and live_gate_caught (Option A confirmed by human, with mapping-table and shared-writer riders)
  @task:TASK-LBL-004
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: A review disposition produces a label record adjacent to the evidence it judges
    Given a task review has reached a disposition with verdict class "operator_caught"
    When the disposition lands
    Then a label record should exist adjacent to the task's evidence artifacts
    And the label record should carry the task id, the feature id, and the verdict class
    And the label record should reference the evidence directory it judges
    And the label record should carry the disposition timestamp

  # Why: Each disposition source maps to its own verdict class — the four-class taxonomy is the contract,
  # and the source-to-class mapping must be an explicit table in the writer, not folklore
  @task:TASK-LBL-004
  @key-example
  Scenario Outline: Each disposition source records its corresponding verdict class
    Given a <source> disposition has been reached for the task
    When the disposition lands
    Then the label record should carry the verdict class "<verdict_class>"

    Examples:
      | source       | verdict_class       |
      | coach-upheld | coach_correct       |
      | operator     | operator_caught     |
      | merge review | merge_review_caught |
      | live gate    | live_gate_caught    |

  # Why: 9F43 rider — labels must join the run identity so Chronicler rows correlate
  @task:TASK-LBL-002
  @key-example
  Scenario: A label record carries the run correlation identity
    Given the evidence artifacts were produced by a run with a known run identity and attempt number
    When a disposition lands for that task
    Then the label record should carry the same run identity as the evidence it judges
    And the label record should carry the attempt number of the judged turn

  # Why: The consumer contract — a harvest joins labels to evidence purely by reading files
  @task:TASK-LBL-004
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: A harvest consumer joins labels to evidence by file read alone
    Given label records exist for several tasks with dispositions
    When a harvest transform reads the label records for a task
    Then it should recover the verdict class, evidence reference, and run identity without consulting any external service
    And it should not require manual retro archaeology to determine the outcome

  # ── GROUP B: Boundary Conditions ──

